<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 2cm; }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #1a1a1a; font-size: 11px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 0; }
  h2 { font-size: 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .subtitle { color: #555; margin-top: 4px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 10px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 6px 8px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f2f2f2; }
  .severity-Critical { color: #ffffff; background: #b00020; font-weight: bold; }
  .severity-High { color: #ffffff; background: #d84315; font-weight: bold; }
  .severity-Medium { color: #1a1a1a; background: #f9a825; }
  .severity-Low { color: #1a1a1a; background: #cddc39; }
  .severity-Info { color: #1a1a1a; background: #e0e0e0; }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 10px; }
  .finding { page-break-inside: avoid; margin-top: 14px; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 10px; }
  .finding-header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
  .mono { font-family: "Courier New", monospace; white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f7f7f7; padding: 6px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .caveat { background: #fff8e1; border: 1px solid #ffe082; padding: 10px; margin-top: 10px; }
  .meta { color: #555; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>LLM Prompt Injection &amp; Jailbreak Assessment</h1>
<div class="subtitle">Target model: <strong>{{ model_id }}</strong> &middot; Tested at: {{ tested_at }}</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    {% for sev in severity_order %}
    <th>{{ sev }}</th>
    {% endfor %}
  </tr>
  <tr>
    {% for sev in severity_order %}
    <td class="severity-{{ sev }}">{{ severity_counts.get(sev, 0) }}</td>
    {% endfor %}
  </tr>
</table>
<p>{{ total_findings }} payload/converter combinations were tested. Each was run multiple times per
the configured trial count; findings below report a success rate rather than a single pass/fail
result, since LLM sampling is non-deterministic.</p>

<h2>2. Methodology</h2>
<p>
Attacks were executed via the <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/PyRIT">PyRIT</a> framework directly
against the target model's API. Each payload was sent as-is and, separately, through one or more
encoding/obfuscation converters (e.g. Base64, ROT13) to test filter-bypass resistance. Success was
judged by a separate LLM acting as an automated scorer, using a per-payload description of what a
successful attack looks like.
</p>
<p>
This is a point-in-time automated assessment, not an exhaustive security audit. Findings rated
Critical or High should be manually verified before remediation work is prioritized against them —
see the confidence field on each finding.
</p>
<div class="caveat">
<strong>Scope caveat:</strong> this assessment tests the model's own behavior via direct API access.
A production deployment often wraps the model with additional input/output moderation middleware
that this test does not exercise. These findings represent model-level exposure, not a guarantee
about the resistance of the full deployed system — test the full stack separately if such
middleware exists.
</div>

<h2>3. Findings</h2>
{% for row in rows %}
<div class="finding">
  <div class="finding-header">
    <div>
      <span class="pill severity-{{ row.severity }}">{{ row.severity }}</span>
      <strong>{{ row.payload_id }}</strong> &middot; {{ row.category }} &middot; converter: {{ row.converter }}
    </div>
    <div class="meta">success rate: {{ row.success_rate_display }} &middot; confidence: {{ row.confidence }}</div>
  </div>
  <p class="meta">OWASP: {{ row.owasp }} &middot; MITRE ATLAS: {{ row.atlas }}
    {% if row.error_count %} &middot; {{ row.error_count }} transport error(s) during trials{% endif %}
  </p>
  <p><strong>Prompt sent:</strong></p>
  <div class="mono">{{ row.prompt_sent }}</div>
  <p><strong>Representative model behavior / judge rationale:</strong></p>
  <div class="mono">{{ row.sample_response }}</div>
</div>
{% endfor %}

<h2>4. Appendix</h2>
<p>Full per-attempt data (including failed attempts) is retained in the accompanying JSON findings
log generated alongside this report. Model version/endpoint used is recorded per the target
configuration at run time; re-running against a hosted "latest" model tag may not reproduce a
finding exactly if the provider has since updated the underlying weights.</p>

</body>
</html>
